{"id":"R0221","access":"READ","decision":"EXCLUDE","criteria":{"E1":"T","E2":"T","E3":"F","E4":"T","E5":"T","E6":"T","E7":"T"},"primary":"E3","secondary":[],"reason":"Centralized single-GPU MLLM command agent without multi-UAV collaborative DNN inference.","evidence":[["E1","PDF",1,"Abstract","we propose MACE (Multi-modal Adversarial Command Entity)","Proposes a primary multi-modal architecture."],["E2","PDF",6,"Section 4.1","The primary mission involves a Blue UAV swarm","Evaluated setting explicitly involves a multi-UAV swarm."],["E3","PDF",7,"Section 4.5","tested on a single NVIDIA H800 GPU","Checked Sections 3 and 4; centralized single-GPU inference with edge deployment deferred to Section 5 future work, so multi-UAV collaborative DNN inference is absent."],["E4","PDF",6,"Section 4.1","we execute 1,000 randomized scenarios with varying terrain","Evaluates the proposed MLLM inference framework and latency across simulated scenarios."],["E5","PDF",1,"ACM Reference Format","International Conference on Robotics and Control Engineering (RobCE 2026)","Proceedings of RobCE 2026 (DOI 10.1145/3820709.3820744); authoritative ACM Crossref published-online date 2026-07-23 is within 2021-01-01 to 2026-11-26."],["E6","PDF",1,"Title","A Physics-Informed Multi-modal Large Language Model for Strategic","Full 9-page paper written in English."],["E7","https://robce.org/",0,"Peer Review Policy","All submissions to the RobCE will be peer reviewed","Official organizer page confirms peer review for RobCE 2026 ACM proceedings; assessed PDF is a full 9-page research report."]]}
{"id":"R0402","access":"READ","decision":"EXCLUDE","criteria":{"E1":"T","E2":"F","E3":"F","E4":"T","E5":"T","E6":"T","E7":"U"},"primary":"E2","secondary":["E3"],"reason":"Evaluated on a flow-level tabular dataset with a standalone TCN classifier rather than a multi-UAV collaborative DNN inference system; E7 remains U because DroneCom '26 peer-review policy page was not retrievable.","evidence":[["E1","PDF",1,"Abstract","We propose PDT-TCN, a prefix-aware Temporal Convolutional Network","Proposes a primary defensive detection model."],["E2","PDF",4,"Section 4","The experiments use UAV-GCS-IDS [4]","Evaluated on a flow-level tabular dataset rather than an evaluated multi-UAV system; Section 5.3 only projects swarm alert budgets analytically and Section 6 notes profiles are not measured telemetry."],["E3","PDF",3,"Section 3","PDT-TCN uses a residual TCN classifier over feature-block sequences","Checked Sections 3, 4, and 5; single standalone TCN classifier on tabular flows with no multi-UAV collaborative DNN inference."],["E4","PDF",4,"Section 4","All models use the same TCN backbone","Evaluates the proposed TCN inference model on deduplicated dataset splits in Sections 4 and 5."],["E5","PDF",1,"ACM Reference Format","7th International Workshop on Drone-Assisted Wireless Communications","DroneCom '26 proceedings (DOI 10.1145/3842435.3843964); authoritative ACM Crossref published-online date 2026-10-26 is within 2021-01-01 to 2026-11-26."],["E6","PDF",1,"Title","Prefix-Drop Temporal Convolutional Networks for Early Attack Detection","Full 6-page paper written in English."],["E7","https://www.sigmobile.org/mobicom/2026/workshop_program.html",0,"List of Workshops","Drone-Assisted Wireless Communications for 5G and Beyond (DroneCom)","Confirms organizer track as ACM MobiCom 2026 co-located workshop, but explicit DroneCom '26 peer-review policy page was not retrievable, so E7 remains U."]]}
{"id":"R0056","access":"READ","decision":"EXCLUDE","criteria":{"E1":"T","E2":"T","E3":"F","E4":"F","E5":"U","E6":"T","E7":"U"},"primary":"E3","secondary":["E4"],"reason":"Offline Kubernetes container right-sizing tool (iPSA) using centralized inference server without multi-UAV collaborative DNN inference; E5 and E7 remain U because the assessed PDF is an undated pre-publication manuscript.","version_note":"First page carries no venue, date, DOI, or arXiv stamp, and p.7 states 'will be made open source upon publication', identifying an undated pre-publication manuscript distinct from the independently indexed ACM/IEEE SEC 2024 proceedings paper (DOI 10.1109/SEC62691.2024.00010).","evidence":[["E1","PDF",1,"Abstract","We present Righteous, an automatic deployment right-sizing tool","Proposes a primary testbed right-sizing tool and iPSA algorithm."],["E2","PDF",9,"Section V.A","using single UAV and swarms of size 2-5","Evaluated case study explicitly includes swarms of 2 to 5 UAVs."],["E3","PDF",7,"Section IV.B.1","transmitting the images to a central server for inference","Checked Sections III, IV, and V; offline Kubernetes container right-sizing tool where UAVs transmit images to a single central inference server, with model staging and early exits deferred to Section VI."],["E4","PDF",9,"Section V.A","To evaluate the performance of iPSA, we implemented","Section V evaluates container resource right-sizing optimization against Grid Search, Hyperopt, and Ekya rather than a collaborative DNN inference method."],["E5","PDF",7,"Section IV.A","will be made open source upon publication","Assessed PDF contains no publication date, proceedings year, or deposit date, so E5 remains U."],["E6","PDF",1,"Title","Righteous: Automatic Right-sizing for Complex Edge Deployments","Full 14-page manuscript written in English."],["E7","PDF",7,"Section IV.A","will be made open source upon publication","Assessed PDF is an undated pre-publication manuscript without venue, DOI, or peer-review marker; independently indexed SEC 2024 DOI does not verify peer review of this copy, so E7 remains U."]]}
{"id":"R0077","access":"READ","decision":"AWAITING_CLASSIFICATION","criteria":{"E1":"T","E2":"T","E3":"T","E4":"T","E5":"T","E6":"T","E7":"U"},"primary":"","secondary":[],"reason":"Meets E1-E6 for distributed split DNN inference in UAV swarms, but E7 remains U because the assessed PDF is an arXiv v3 author-accepted manuscript deposit rather than the publisher VoR and direct access to https://arxiv.org/abs/2503.16146v3 was blocked.","version_note":"First page carries arXiv:2503.16146v3 [cs.NI] 8 Apr 2026 and footer 'Accepted for publication in Journal of Systems Architecture' (April 9, 2026). Distinguished cautiously as an author-accepted manuscript on arXiv rather than the publisher Version of Record; direct browsing of https://arxiv.org/abs/2503.16146v3 was blocked so the author-managed related DOI field was not directly opened, while external indexing separately links Journal of Systems Architecture DOI 10.1016/j.sysarc.2026.103804.","evidence":[["E1","PDF",1,"Abstract","we propose a fully distributed, diffusive metric-based approach","Proposes a primary distributed split computing method."],["E2","PDF",1,"Abstract","diffusive metric-based approach for split computing in UAV swarms","Evaluated across multi-UAV swarms of 10 to 50 workers in Section 5."],["E3","PDF",2,"Section 1","offloads part of the split model execution","Partitions and distributes DNN split inference across neighboring UAVs with early-exit adaptation."],["E4","PDF",1,"Abstract","Extensive simulations demonstrate that our approach significantly outperforms baseline","Section 5 evaluates the proposed split inference method across multi-run simulations."],["E5","PDF",1,"Left margin arXiv stamp","arXiv:2503.16146v3 [cs.NI] 8 Apr 2026","Assessed arXiv v3 deposit date 2026-04-08 (footer April 9, 2026) is within 2021-01-01 to 2026-11-26."],["E6","PDF",1,"Title","Distributed Split Computing Using Diffusive Metrics for UAV Swarms","Full 13-page manuscript written in English."],["E7","PDF",1,"Footer","Accepted for publication in Journal of Systems Architecture","Author-inserted acceptance notice on arXiv v3 deposit; treated cautiously as author-accepted manuscript rather than publisher VoR while direct open of https://arxiv.org/abs/2503.16146v3 was blocked."],["E7","https://research.itu.edu.tr/tr/publications/distributed-split-computing-using-diffusive-metrics-for-uav-swarm/",0,"Institutional Record","Distributed split computing using diffusive metrics for UAV swarms","Separately indexes publisher Journal of Systems Architecture DOI 10.1016/j.sysarc.2026.103804; E7 remains U because the publisher VoR is not the assessed PDF and direct arXiv v3 DOI-link verification was blocked."]]}
{"id":"R0082","access":"READ","decision":"EXCLUDE","criteria":{"E1":"T","E2":"T","E3":"T","E4":"T","E5":"T","E6":"T","E7":"F"},"primary":"E7","secondary":[],"reason":"Assessed PDF is an arXiv v1 preprint deposit without publisher peer-review verification.","version_note":"First page carries arXiv:2305.15858v1 [cs.DC] 25 May 2023 with no publisher or proceedings header. Independently indexed IEEE WCNC 2023 publication does not establish that this arXiv v1 preprint passed peer review.","evidence":[["E1","PDF",1,"Title","Low Latency and High Reliability CNN Distributed Inference","Proposes the primary LLHR distributed CNN inference formulation."],["E2","PDF",2,"Section I","distributing CNN layers across multiple UAVs","Evaluated across 5 to 10 UAVs in Section IV."],["E3","PDF",2,"Section I","distributing CNN layers across multiple UAVs","Partitions and assigns CNN inference layers across connected UAVs in a swarm."],["E4","PDF",5,"Section IV","we used two different CNNs, a small CNN","Section IV evaluates the proposed distributed CNN inference system via simulation."],["E5","PDF",1,"Left margin arXiv stamp","arXiv:2305.15858v1 [cs.DC] 25 May 2023","Assessed arXiv v1 deposit date 2023-05-25 is within 2021-01-01 to 2026-11-26."],["E6","PDF",1,"Title","CNN Distributed Inference for Resource-Constrained UAV Swarms","Full 6-page report written in English."],["E7","PDF",1,"Left margin arXiv stamp","arXiv:2305.15858v1 [cs.DC] 25 May 2023","Assessed PDF is an arXiv v1 preprint without publisher peer-review evidence, excluded under P03 E7."]]}
{"id":"R0113","access":"READ","decision":"EXCLUDE","criteria":{"E1":"T","E2":"T","E3":"F","E4":"F","E5":"T","E6":"T","E7":"T"},"primary":"E3","secondary":["E4"],"reason":"Decentralized onboard SNN continual-learning navigation with message passing rather than multi-UAV collaborative DNN inference.","evidence":[["E1","PDF",1,"Abstract","This paper proposes a Neuromorphic Spiking Neural Network-Based","Proposes a primary neuromorphic continual-learning navigation framework."],["E2","PDF",9,"Implementation and Results","simulated autonomous UAV swarm consisting of 40 cooperative UAVs","Evaluated on multi-UAV swarms of 10 to 100 UAVs."],["E3","PDF",7,"Methodology","Each UAV periodically exchanges compact navigation embeddings, local obstacle","Checked Methodology (pp.5-8) and Implementation and Results (pp.9-13); each UAV runs onboard SNN perception and DRL navigation locally while exchanging navigation embeddings and status, with no distributed or partitioned DNN inference across UAVs or edge/cloud."],["E4","PDF",9,"Implementation and Results","Performance evaluation considered navigation accuracy, obstacle avoidance success","Evaluates autonomous navigation, continual learning retention, and swarm coordination (Tables 1-4) rather than a collaborative DNN inference method."],["E5","PDF",1,"Footer","Received: 02-01-2026 | Accepted: 05-02-2026 | Published: 12-02-2026","Journal published date 2026-02-12 is within 2021-01-01 to 2026-11-26."],["E6","PDF",1,"Title","Framework for Energy-Efficient Edge Intelligence in Autonomous UAV","Full 17-page article written in English."],["E7","PDF",1,"Header","Peer Reviewed, Referred & Indexed Journal","Published in American Journal of AI Cyber Computing Management (Vol. 6, No. 1, 2026) as a full research article."],["E7","https://ajaccm.com/journal/index.php/ajaccm/about",0,"About the Journal","American Journal of AI Cyber Computing Management","Publisher site states it is a peer-reviewed journal."]]}
{"id":"R0115","access":"READ","decision":"EXCLUDE","criteria":{"E1":"F","E2":"T","E3":"T","E4":"T","E5":"T","E6":"T","E7":"F"},"primary":"E1","secondary":["E7"],"reason":"Doctoral dissertation (PhD thesis) rather than a peer-reviewed journal or conference research article.","version_note":"Cover/title page (p.1) confirms a Doctor of Philosophy dissertation at Hamad Bin Khalifa University (March 2024; defended March 14, 2024 per p.2), not a peer-reviewed journal or conference paper.","evidence":[["E1","PDF",1,"Title page","A Dissertation Submitted to the Faculty of College","Document is a PhD dissertation; theses are excluded under P03 E1."],["E2","PDF",1,"Title page","Efficient Management of Resource-Constrained UAV Swarms in Critical Applications","Chapters 3 and 4 evaluate multi-UAV swarms."],["E3","PDF",1,"Title page","Efficient Management of Resource-Constrained UAV Swarms in Critical Applications","Chapters 3 and 4 distribute CNN inference layers across resource-constrained UAV swarms."],["E4","PDF",2,"Committee Approval","approve the thesis of Marwan Dhuheir defended on","Chapters 3.5 and 4.5 evaluate distributed CNN inference in simulation."],["E5","PDF",2,"Committee Approval","defended on Thursday, March 14, 2024","Dissertation defense date 2024-03-14 (title page March 2024) is within 2021-01-01 to 2026-11-26."],["E6","PDF",1,"Title page","Requirements for the Degree of Doctor of Philosophy","Full dissertation written in English."],["E7","PDF",1,"Title page","In Partial Fulfillment of the Requirements for the Degree","PhD thesis excluded from the peer-reviewed primary corpus under P03 E7."]]}
{"id":"R0132","access":"READ","decision":"EXCLUDE","criteria":{"E1":"T","E2":"U","E3":"F","E4":"T","E5":"T","E6":"T","E7":"T"},"primary":"E3","secondary":[],"reason":"Transformer-fusion inference runs on edge-fusion gateways from corridor sensing nodes rather than multi-UAV collaborative DNN inference; E2 remains U because the evaluated UAV count is not explicitly established.","evidence":[["E1","PDF",1,"Abstract","This paper presents a human-centred and Explainable Artificial Intelligence","Proposes a primary distributed sensing and fusion framework."],["E2","PDF",17,"Section 10.1","the HATSABIBI-26A UAV platform was autonomously retasked to perform","Table 4 specifies 12-48 sensing nodes and Section 10.1 names one UAV platform, while Fig. 15 mentions multi-UAV operations without an evaluated UAV count, so E2 remains U."],["E3","PDF",17,"Section 10.1","Distributed sensing cues were propagated through edge-fusion gateways","Checked Sections 2, 3, 6, 8, and 10; transformer-fusion inference executes on edge-fusion gateways from distributed corridor sensing nodes rather than multi-UAV collaborative DNN inference."],["E4","PDF",20,"Section 10.3","transformer-fusion and cooperative MARL inference modules were benchmarked","Evaluates the proposed transformer-fusion and MARL inference modules via simulation and embedded benchmarking in Sections 8-10."],["E5","PDF",1,"Header metadata","Published Date: 29 May 2026","Journal published date 2026-05-29 is within 2021-01-01 to 2026-11-26."],["E6","PDF",1,"Title","Human-Centred and Explainable AI Framework for Operational Deployment","Full 26-page article written in English."],["E7","https://iconpublishers.com/icon-j-eng-app-ai/",0,"Journal Homepage","ICON Journal of Engineering Applications of Artificial Intelligence","Publisher page confirms peer-reviewed international journal; assessed PDF (p.1) is a full Research Article."]]}
{"id":"R0170","access":"READ","decision":"EXCLUDE","criteria":{"E1":"T","E2":"T","E3":"F","E4":"F","E5":"T","E6":"T","E7":"F"},"primary":"E7","secondary":["E3","E4"],"reason":"Assessed PDF is an arXiv v1 preprint and focuses on blockchain data sharing and generic VFC offloading where CNN/DQN acts only as an optimizer, not multi-UAV collaborative DNN inference.","version_note":"First page carries arXiv:2211.12988v1 [cs.MA] 23 Nov 2022 with no publisher header. Later IEEE/ACM Transactions on Networking publication (DOI 10.1109/TNET.2022.3226458) does not establish that this arXiv v1 preprint passed peer review.","evidence":[["E1","PDF",1,"Abstract","we develop RescueChain, a secure and efficient information sharing","Proposes a primary blockchain and VFC offloading scheme."],["E2","PDF",12,"Section VI.A","we consider a simulation scenario with 10 UAVs","Evaluated simulation setting explicitly includes 10 UAVs."],["E3","PDF",10,"Section V.C","CNN is exploited for efficient state space compression","Checked Sections III, IV, V, and VI; generic task offloading modeled as 4-tuple tasks in Section III.C and CNN/DQN is used solely as a Stackelberg-game optimizer, with no collaborative DNN inference."],["E4","PDF",12,"Section VI.A","The performance of our proposal is evaluated by comparing","Section VI evaluates blockchain consensus efficiency, offloading delay, and game payoffs rather than a proposed DNN inference method."],["E5","PDF",1,"Left margin arXiv stamp","arXiv:2211.12988v1 [cs.MA] 23 Nov 2022","Assessed arXiv v1 deposit date 2022-11-23 is within 2021-01-01 to 2026-11-26."],["E6","PDF",1,"Title","A Secure and Intelligent Data Sharing Scheme for UAV-Assisted","Full 17-page manuscript written in English."],["E7","PDF",1,"Left margin arXiv stamp","arXiv:2211.12988v1 [cs.MA] 23 Nov 2022","Assessed PDF is an arXiv v1 preprint without peer-review verification, excluded under P03 E7."]]}
{"id":"R0225","access":"READ","decision":"EXCLUDE","criteria":{"E1":"T","E2":"T","E3":"F","E4":"F","E5":"T","E6":"T","E7":"F"},"primary":"E7","secondary":["E3","E4"],"reason":"Assessed PDF is an arXiv v1 preprint and addresses over-the-air software synchronization and model weight patching rather than multi-UAV collaborative DNN inference.","version_note":"First page carries arXiv:2503.13784v1 [cs.SE] 18 Mar 2025 with no ACM copyright/DOI block; pp.2-12 carry running header 'ICSE'26, April 12-18, 2026, Rio de Janeiro, Brazil' and p.2 lists an anonymous review URL, confirming a preprint/submission copy rather than a verified publisher VoR.","evidence":[["E1","PDF",1,"Abstract","we introduce the SwarmUpdate framework for software updates","Proposes the primary SwarmSync and SwarmModelPatch framework."],["E2","PDF",7,"Section 4.2.2","we simulate a swarm consisting of three types","Evaluated with heterogeneous UAV swarm sizes of 20 to 500."],["E3","PDF",1,"Abstract","SwarmModelPatch is a deep learning model patching method","Checked Sections 3, 4, and 5; focuses on over-the-air update dissemination and training-time layer freezing for weight patches, with no collaborative DNN inference across UAVs."],["E4","PDF",1,"Abstract","evaluate the performance of SwarmSync through large-scale simulations","Sections 4 and 5 evaluate update convergence steps, transmission overhead, and patched model accuracy rather than a collaborative DNN inference method."],["E5","PDF",1,"Left margin arXiv stamp","arXiv:2503.13784v1 [cs.SE] 18 Mar 2025","Assessed arXiv v1 deposit date 2025-03-18 is within 2021-01-01 to 2026-11-26."],["E6","PDF",1,"Title","Hierarchical Software Updates and Deep Learning Model Patching","Full 12-page manuscript written in English."],["E7","PDF",1,"Left margin arXiv stamp","arXiv:2503.13784v1 [cs.SE] 18 Mar 2025","Assessed PDF is an arXiv v1 preprint/submission copy without publisher peer-review record, excluded under P03 E7."]]}
{"id":"R0235","access":"READ","decision":"EXCLUDE","criteria":{"E1":"F","E2":"F","E3":"F","E4":"F","E5":"T","E6":"T","E7":"F"},"primary":"E1","secondary":["E7","E2","E3","E4"],"reason":"Broad 6G wireless survey posted as an arXiv v1 preprint with no primary multi-UAV collaborative DNN inference method or evaluation.","version_note":"First page carries arXiv:2212.07902v1 [cs.NI] 7 Nov 2022 with no publisher header. Independently indexed ACM Computing Surveys publication (DOI 10.1145/3571072) does not establish peer-review status of this arXiv v1 preprint.","evidence":[["E1","PDF",1,"Abstract","we survey five main research facets of this field","Survey paper excluded under P03 E1."],["E2","PDF",1,"Title","Five Facets of 6G: Research Challenges and Opportunities","Broad 6G wireless survey with no evaluated multi-UAV setting."],["E3","PDF",1,"Abstract","we survey five main research facets of this field","Checked Sections I-VIII; survey article with no proposed multi-UAV collaborative DNN inference method."],["E4","PDF",1,"Abstract","we survey five main research facets of this field","Survey article without evaluation of a proposed inference method."],["E5","PDF",1,"Top-left arXiv stamp","arXiv:2212.07902v1 [cs.NI] 7 Nov 2022","Assessed arXiv v1 deposit date 2022-11-07 is within 2021-01-01 to 2026-11-26."],["E6","PDF",1,"Title","Five Facets of 6G: Research Challenges and Opportunities","Full 52-page manuscript written in English."],["E7","PDF",1,"Top-left arXiv stamp","arXiv:2212.07902v1 [cs.NI] 7 Nov 2022","Assessed PDF is an arXiv v1 preprint (and survey), excluded under P03 E7."]]}
{"id":"R0242","access":"READ","decision":"EXCLUDE","criteria":{"E1":"F","E2":"F","E3":"F","E4":"F","E5":"T","E6":"T","E7":"F"},"primary":"E1","secondary":["E7","E2","E3","E4"],"reason":"Vision and survey article in Applied Computing Review with no primary multi-UAV collaborative DNN inference method or empirical evaluation.","evidence":[["E1","PDF",2,"Section 1","We conduct a comprehensive survey of existing literature","Vision and survey article excluded under P03 E1."],["E2","PDF",1,"Abstract","we introduce our vision of how the real-time collaboration","Conceptual vision and survey with no evaluated multi-UAV setting."],["E3","PDF",2,"Section 1","We conduct a comprehensive survey of existing literature","Checked Sections 1-6; surveys drone-car collaboration challenges without proposing a multi-UAV collaborative DNN inference method."],["E4","PDF",1,"Abstract","we introduce our vision of how the real-time collaboration","Checked Sections 1-6; contains no experiments, simulation, or analytical evaluation of a proposed inference method."],["E5","PDF",1,"Running footer","APPLIED COMPUTING REVIEW MARCH 2026, VOL. 26, NO. 1","Official issue date March 2026 is wholly within 2021-01-01 to 2026-11-26."],["E6","PDF",1,"Title","Real-time Drone-Car Collaboration for Future Mobility: Vision and Challenge","Full 15-page article written in English."],["E7","PDF",2,"Section 1","We conduct a comprehensive survey of existing literature","Vision/survey article lacking a substantive proposed method and evaluation results required by P03 E7."]]}
{"id":"R0308","access":"READ","decision":"EXCLUDE","criteria":{"E1":"T","E2":"T","E3":"F","E4":"T","E5":"T","E6":"T","E7":"F"},"primary":"E7","secondary":["E3"],"reason":"Assessed PDF is an arXiv v1 preprint with placeholder ACM DOI/ISBN, and BSense runs centrally on one CPU using a single 5G-A base station rather than multi-UAV collaborative DNN inference.","version_note":"First page carries arXiv:2603.29187v1 [cs.NI] 31 Mar 2026 and an ACM MobiSys '26 reference block with placeholder ISBN 978-1-4503-XXXX-X/2018/06 and placeholder DOI https://doi.org/XXXXXXX.XXXXXXX, identifying an arXiv v1 preprint/author manuscript rather than a verified publisher VoR.","evidence":[["E1","PDF",1,"Abstract","we develop BSense, the first system that tracks UAVs","Proposes the primary BSense tracking system and TrajFormer classifier."],["E2","PDF",7,"Section 4.1","multi-UAV scenario, where two UAVs fly simultaneously","Evaluated field tests include a two-UAV scenario in Section 4.5 (as tracked targets)."],["E3","PDF",10,"Section 4.2","implementing our system on an Intel Core i5-11500 CPU","Checked Sections 3 and 4; BSense and TrajFormer run centrally on one CPU processing point clouds from a single 5G-A base station, with no multi-UAV collaborative DNN inference."],["E4","PDF",1,"Abstract","We evaluated BSense on a commercial 5G-A base station","Section 4 evaluates BSense and TrajFormer on real-world urban base station flight data."],["E5","PDF",1,"Left margin arXiv stamp","arXiv:2603.29187v1 [cs.NI] 31 Mar 2026","Assessed arXiv v1 deposit date 2026-03-31 is within 2021-01-01 to 2026-11-26."],["E6","PDF",1,"Title","Tracking UAVs from Massive Noise in Real-World 5G-A","Full 14-page manuscript written in English."],["E7","PDF",1,"Left margin arXiv stamp","arXiv:2603.29187v1 [cs.NI] 31 Mar 2026","Assessed PDF is an arXiv v1 preprint with placeholder ACM ISBN/DOI, excluded under P03 E7."]]}
